  "summary": "Four studies directly apply federated learning (decentralised training without pooled records) to customer churn (predicting customer attrition), and one applies a multilevel probabilistic model to the same topic. [V0201] (Chen et al., 2019) evaluates on ChurnBench, reporting accuracy 0.78. [V0203] (El-Sayed et al., 2021) evaluates on Atlas-ICU, reporting AUROC 0.92 — the strongest result among the federated approaches. [V0202] (Duarte et al., 2020) evaluates on MetroFlow, reporting MAE 0.85. [V0204] (Fischer et al., 2022) evaluates on AgriSat-4, reporting F1 0.64. [V0211] (Gupta et al., 2023) applies multilevel probabilistic models with partial pooling to customer attrition on Atlas-ICU, achieving accuracy 0.79; while not federated learning, it is the next most relevant study directly targeting the churn topic. Documents such as [V0052] and [V0101] mention federated learning for churn only as prior work and are therefore not directly relevant. Documents addressing other topics (fraud detection, agricultural yield, battery life, traffic flow, hate speech, sepsis) are excluded regardless of method.",
